internal/core/service/blocklist.txt
===================================

Derived from a list of common passwords in SecLists
(https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists), file
Passwords/Common-Credentials/100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt at commit
4c0fd59432ab8508edc23b3c880127edb12e34d5, fetched on 2026-10-23.
SHA-256 of the downloaded file:
c2e5696882c603b76bb67a47ee970897e5a76fc4c3f5547abe3d0ca340c576e0.

Licence of the source: the SecLists repository is licensed under the MIT License (Copyright (c)
2018 Daniel Miessler; full text below). The file itself carries no separate licence or
provenance note: the directory README of Passwords/Common-Credentials does not mention it, and
the repository README states that the whole project is licensed under the MIT licence.

Caveat: the original publisher of this list (the UK National Cyber Security Centre) does not state a
licence for it in SecLists. It is used here under SecLists' repository-wide MIT licence, which the
project owner accepted on 2026-10-23. Re-check the upstream terms before any commercial use.

Filtering (service.FilterBlocklistEntry): lower-cased; only entries of 6-32 printable ASCII
characters without spaces that contain at least one letter and one special character are kept;
duplicates are removed; the result is sorted. An entry that fails these rules can never equal a
password our policy accepts, so leaving it out does not change which passwords are rejected.

Rebuild:
  curl -fsSL -o /tmp/source.txt https://raw.githubusercontent.com/danielmiessler/SecLists/4c0fd59432ab8508edc23b3c880127edb12e34d5/Passwords/Common-Credentials/100k-most-used-passwords-NCSC.txt
  go run scripts/build_blocklist.go -in /tmp/source.txt -out internal/core/service/blocklist.txt

